<title>UK: Carlton chairman back at work after assault.</title>
<headline>Carlton chairman back at work after assault.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carlton Communications Plc chairman Michael Green is back at work and &quot;absolutely fine&quot; after being stabbed in an assault on Tuesday night, a source close to the company said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;He is absolutely fine and back at work,&quot; she said, but declined to give further details.</p>
<p>Green and his wife were attacked outside their home in Mayfair, central London, reports said.</p>
<p>Carlton shares were unchanged at 506-1/2p.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
